# Keep the build context small, and keep HOST artefacts out of the image.
#
# node_modules above all: the image installs its own (linux/arm64 or amd64
# binaries). Copying the host's tree over it would overwrite the installed one
# with binaries built for another platform.
#
# `node_modules` on its own matches ONLY the root one: .dockerignore uses Go's
# filepath.Match, where a pattern without `**` never crosses a directory
# boundary. The nested trees (publication/server_api/v2, publication/site_builder)
# are the big ones — leaving them in put ~320 MB of foreign-platform binaries in
# the context and the image, which is exactly what the paragraph above forbids.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
.github
rewrite
test
docs/site
site
private
*.log
.DS_Store

# The generated media rule files and any local media/private trees never belong
# in an image — they are runtime state on a volume.
media
